# Composable UI

- Build features from semantic, focused components with clear props and explicit state ownership.
- Prefer children, slots and composition over deeply nested conditional variants and many boolean flags.
- Separate reusable primitives (layout, buttons, typography) from business-specific components (event cards, booking forms).
- Use a single source for brand colors, spacing and type roles; avoid one-off design values without reason.
- Keep responsive behavior within the component design. Test narrow/mobile, tablet and desktop.
- Support keyboard operation, focus-visible, reduced motion, sufficient contrast, semantic headings and accessible form feedback.
- Implement real loading, empty, error, success and disabled states for interactive workflows.
- Use stable keys and semantic link/button elements. Don't use click handlers on decorative containers.
- Avoid expensive client components where server components can render the same result.
